# pointsfromblobs

- Label: Points from Blobs
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 3 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pointsfromblobs.html
- Summary (EN): The Points From Blobs node finds connected bright or dark regions in a mono layer using a threshold, and places one point at the centre of each region.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Points From Blobs place un point au centre de chaque zone connectée située au-dessus ou au-dessous d'un seuil, sans que la page précise le calcul du centre.

- Inputs meaning: ["blobs: mono layer to generate points from; the only input"]

- Key parameters: ["Blob when: whether pixel groups above or below the threshold count as blobs", "Threshold: cut-off value deciding which pixels belong to a blob", "Space: coordinate space of the output points: Image, Texture, Pixel or World"]

- Caveats: ["The page does not say how a blob centre is computed (centroid or bounding-box centre).", "It does not explain how touching or overlapping blobs are handled.", "It lists no default parameter values.", "Available since Houdini 22.0."]

